import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 363 | Dou Continent · Decomposing Tang San's Predatory Thinking: Institutional Predation of Soul-Ring Hunting","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 363 | Dou Continent · Decomposing Tang San's Predatory Thinking: Institutional Predation of Soul-Ring Hunting","no":363,"module":2,"tags":["Dou Continent","Tang San","Predatory Thinking","Soul-Ring Hunting","Institutional Predation"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","58-Twin-Soul Ethics Guidelines"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0363_模块2-斗罗-唐三掠夺思维拆解-魂环猎杀的制度性掠夺.md","filePath":"en/0363_模块2-斗罗-唐三掠夺思维拆解-魂环猎杀的制度性掠夺.md"}`),s={name:"en/0363_模块2-斗罗-唐三掠夺思维拆解-魂环猎杀的制度性掠夺.md"};function a(r,e,l,u,h,d){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-363-dou-continent-·-decomposing-tang-san-s-predatory-thinking-institutional-predation-of-soul-ring-hunting" tabindex="-1">Entry 363 | Dou Continent · Decomposing Tang San&#39;s Predatory Thinking: Institutional Predation of Soul-Ring Hunting <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-363-dou-continent-·-decomposing-tang-san-s-predatory-thinking-institutional-predation-of-soul-ring-hunting" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 363 | Dou Continent · Decomposing Tang San&#39;s Predatory Thinking: Institutional Predation of Soul-Ring Hunting&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dou Continent System Decomposition (Entry 4) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 19, 58</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-predation-is-written-into-the-two-words-level-up" tabindex="-1">Introduction: When predation is written into the two words &quot;level up&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-predation-is-written-into-the-two-words-level-up" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: When predation is written into the two words &quot;level up&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The anti-predation axiom&#39;s core is: do not use killing-and-plundering as the evolution path. The most special thing about Dou Continent is that its predation is not some villain&#39;s evil deed, but the legal procedure written into every leveling up — a Soul Master who wants to advance must go to the forest to hunt a soul beast, strip off its Origin soul ring cultivated over hundreds or thousands of years. Tang San is merely this system&#39;s most excellent executor. This entry, taking the law-first axiom as core, decomposes how this &quot;institutional predation&quot; is internalized into geniuses&#39; instinct. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: <strong>high (gift-style leaning oligarchic)</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Hunting = loss</strong>: every breakthrough consumes a soul beast&#39;s century-spanning Origin, and the soul beast&#39;s cultivation also consumed the plane&#39;s Origin — this is double loss, not transformation</li><li><strong>Efficiency mismatch</strong>: a soul beast&#39;s thousand-year bitter cultivation is &quot;transformed&quot; by a human hunt into a one-tier soul ring; energy utilization extremely low</li><li><strong>Endowments spinning empty</strong>: Tang San&#39;s past-life Tang Sect hidden weapons and profound skills could have developed into a &quot;non-killing&quot; technical path, but the soul-ring system forces him back to the old hunting road</li></ul><p>Conclusion: treating &quot;killing&quot; as leveling fuel is the greatest waste in the energy loop.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Predation internalized</strong>: when predation is a legal procedure, generations of cultivators all believe &quot;becoming strong = killing&quot;; no one questions the underlying law</li><li><strong>Ecological backlash</strong>: high-tier soul beasts are hunted extinct first; latecomers can only hunt low-tier ones; the overall cultivation ceiling moves down with declining stock</li><li><strong>Moral regression</strong>: humans are taught from childhood that soul beasts are &quot;soul rings&quot;; the view of life is systematically reshaped; Myriad-Rank reconciliation forever impossible</li></ul><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-this-entry-s-core" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (This Entry&#39;s Core) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-this-entry-s-core" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (This Entry&#39;s Core)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang San&#39;s predatory thinking has a three-layer structure:</p><ol><li><strong>Instrumentalizing the other</strong>: in his eyes a soul beast is first &quot;which ring, what years, what attribute,&quot; and only secondarily a living being — this is the predator&#39;s most fundamental cognitive distortion</li><li><strong>Rationalizing killing</strong>: he does not feel he is killing, but feels he is &quot;doing a quest, gathering rings&quot;; moral sense is entirely absorbed by procedure</li><li><strong>Institutional inheritance</strong>: after becoming a god, he does not reform this hunting system, but maintains it — because this system is precisely the source of his legitimacy for reaching the top</li></ol><p>Key insight: Tang San is not &quot;a good person forced to kill,&quot; but &quot;a genius trained by institutions to no longer treat killing as a problem.&quot; This is precisely where institutional predation is most horrifying — it does not require you to be evil, only requires you to look on with indifference.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dou Institutional Predation</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hunt soul beasts for Origin</td><td>Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings: generate Origin rings via man-made Dao laws, kill no beast throughout</td></tr><tr><td>Soul beast = soul ring</td><td>Soul beast as one of Myriad Ranks, equally evolves via self-generation self-growth evolution law</td></tr><tr><td>Killing rationalized</td><td>Cultivation ethics and boundaries written into charter; develop increment, do not consume stock</td></tr><tr><td>Strong ones maintain old system</td><td>Lin Hao path: a victim of old rules awakens then overturns old rules, reconstructs rules</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The alternative&#39;s crux: rewrite &quot;kill one beast to level one&quot; as &quot;cultivate one Dao-Law to nurture Myriad Ranks.&quot;</p><p>The bottom-extinguishing of this institutional predation is precisely Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings: when soul rings can be man-made, the thinking of &quot;treating soul beasts as consumables&quot; loses its institutional soil. Lin Hao, as a victim of old rules, demonstrates another kind of genius — he does not treat the other as a material library to inventory attributes, but condenses the Origin needed for breakthrough from his own Dao Origin; each ring need not be taken, killing is no longer a legal procedure. This is precisely the way to root predation out of geniuses&#39; instinct.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate the Dou &quot;hunt—absorb&quot; procedure</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Group A maintain hunting; Group B inject Path D man-made Dao-Law soul rings</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: soul-beast population count, human breakthrough success rate, Myriad-Rank conflict intensity</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: quantify the civilization benefit after switching from &quot;institutional predation&quot; to &quot;institutional symbiosis&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. Late patches like &quot;spirit souls&quot; and &quot;spirit-soul ring fusion&quot; are essentially partial retcons of early &quot;must hunt&quot;</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong>. To ease hunting controversy, the author keeps patching, but never touches the underlying &quot;killing to level&quot; law</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high</strong></li></ul><p>The most insidious part of institutional predation is that it makes geniuses executors without realizing it. Every time Tang San murmurs &quot;which ring, what attribute&quot; before hunting, he has already reduced another being to data. What Heng Yuan Zhou wants to dismantle is precisely this cognitive distortion: when the other is first a life, and only secondarily a resource, predation loses soil at the human-heart level.</p><p>Look at institutional predation along the causal chain: what Tang San&#39;s generation hunts is the soul beast&#39;s Origin cultivated over a hundred or thousand years; and this soul beast could have continued to evolve and feed back to the plane&#39;s ecology. One hunt simultaneously erases a future high-tier life and a stretch of plane Origin that could have accumulated. The predator thinks he has earned a ring, but actually loses an entire future energy flow — this is the deep cost of the negative-sum loop.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: killing to level is double energy loss</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: predation written into leveling legal procedure, internalized into instinct</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s predation is &quot;privately hoarded knowledge&quot;; Tang San&#39;s predation is &quot;killing to seize Origin&quot; — the latter is harder, more irreversible</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: institutional predation first erases soul beasts&#39; life subjectivity</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: a system that treats killing as fuel cannot symbiose with any external civilization</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang San&#39;s hand is steady, his blade fast, his road smooth — the problem lies in the road itself. Heng Yuan Zhou does not judge every soul beast he killed, only points out one thing: when leveling must step on other races&#39; bones, no matter how glorious this road is, it is a dead end.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dou Continent · decomposing Tang San&#39;s predatory thinking · institutional predation of soul-ring hunting described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./364_模块2-斗罗-魂环体系批判-猎杀魂兽夺本源的掠夺本质.html">Entry 364 · Soul-Ring System Critique</a> · <a href="./377_模块2-斗罗-D路线替代方案-人族人造道则魂环.html">Entry 377 · Path D Alternative</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const m=t(s,[["render",a]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
